<title>SWEDEN: Support for EMU inches up in Sweden - poll.</title>
<headline>Support for EMU inches up in Sweden - poll.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1997-01-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Public support for Sweden's early entry into the Economic and Monetary Union (EMU) has increased but opponents to EMU still dominate, a poll released on Wednesday showed.</p>
<p>A January poll by the Swedish Institute of Public Opinion and Research (SIFO) found 23 percent of people surveyed were in favour of Sweden joining EMU at its start in 1999, compared to 18 percent in a similar survey in November.</p>
<p>Results showed 23 percent thought Sweden should join at a later stage. However, 39 percent remained opposed to membership. The rest were undecided, said the poll published by financial daily newspaper FinansTidningen</p>
<p>-- Belinda Goldsmith, Stockholm newsroom +46-8-700-1045</p>
